Mephistopheles, called Mephi, was a fourth-generation [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] who went among the people of [[Geography/Ushas/index|Ushas]] as the Patchwork Prince: a curious man who travelled on a floating island and was renowned as a legendary tailor. He was a dealmaker.

When [[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]] distrusted him and slipped into his home, Dorcan found a strange book made of patchwork. The Prince appeared before him, cursed him with a mark, revealed himself as an otherworldly entity, and let Dorcan go only on his promise to perform three great labours of Mephi's choosing at some time in the future.

He taught [[People/Dahl|Dahl]] his necromancy and gave him the spell that unravelled Ushas's [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]]. [[Org/Sacrament|Sacrament]] served him as a god and set out to kill Ushas's three [[Divinity/Higher Kind|Higher Kind]], destroying the crystal sphere so that Mephistopheles could eat its life force and ascend from the fourth generation to something greater. He sat in the [[Geography/Ushas/Far Realms|Far Realms of Ushas]]. The party that would found [[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] ([[People/Dorcan|Dorcan]], [[People/Zugg|Zugg]], [[People/Rotok|Rotok]] and [[People/Althane/The Broker|T3C]]) destroyed Sacrament and pinned Mephistopheles with the golden needle from the eleventh floor of the [[Geography/Ushas/Undermountain|Undermountain]], killing him.
